  "Notes": [
    {
      "Text": "Security update for mozilla-nss",
      "Title": "Topic",
      "Type": "Summary"
    },
    {
      "Text": "This update for mozilla-nss fixes the following issue:\n\n- remove compromised eMudhra Intermediates CA (bsc#1286261).\n\nChanges for mozilla-nss:\n\n- update to NSS 3.125.1 (bsc#1289144):\n * bmo#2088196 - backport nssckbi 2.92.\n * bmo#2082793 - Don't cache sessions when ECH was rejected.\n * bmo#2082792 - Keep DTLS handshake messages whole in the send buffer.\n * bmo#2082077 - Initialize sftk_MACCtx in sftk_MAC_Init.\n * bmo#2082027 - reorder session context setup in sftk_doMACInit.\n * bmo#2054723 - harden against integer overflows in lowpbe.c.\n * bmo#2054697 - fix AES GCM parameter serialization in pk11_GetPBECryptoMechanism.\n * bmo#2054695 - handle HMAC truncation when using PK11_Digest* APIs.\n * bmo#2054616 - reject short ciphertexts in sec_pkcs5_rc2.\n",
      "Title": "Details",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "The CVRF data is provided by SUSE under the Creative Commons License 4.0 with Attribution (CC-BY-4.0).",
